The point $P(0.8,\,0.6747)$ lies on the graph of $y=\arctan x$ shown.
Which point must also lie on this graph?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.7cm, y=1.3cm]
\draw[->] (-4.6,0) -- (4.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.2) -- (0,2.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dashed] (-4.4,1.5708) -- (4.4,1.5708);
\draw[dashed] (-4.4,-1.5708) -- (4.4,-1.5708);
\draw[thick,<->,domain=-4.4:4.4,samples=100,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{rad(atan(\x))});
\fill (0.8,0.6747) circle (2pt);
\node[below right,font=\small] at (0.9,0.62) {$P$};
\node[font=\small,above] at (-3.0,1.5708) {$y=\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\node[font=\small,below] at (-3.0,-1.5708) {$y=-\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\node[font=\small] at (2.9,0.35) {$y=\arctan x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

