The graphs of $y=\arcsin x$ and $y=\arctan x$ are shown for $-1\le x\le1$.
How should $f(x)=\arcsin x+\arctan x$ be classified?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.7cm, y=1.2cm]
\draw[->] (-1.5,0) -- (1.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.9) -- (0,2.1) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,domain=-1.5708:1.5708,samples=80,smooth,variable=\t] plot ({sin(deg(\t))},{\t});
\draw[thick,blue,dashed,domain=-1:1,samples=80,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{rad(atan(\x))});
\fill (1,1.5708) circle (1.6pt);
\fill (-1,-1.5708) circle (1.6pt);
\fill[blue] (1,0.7854) circle (1.6pt);
\fill[blue] (-1,-0.7854) circle (1.6pt);
\draw (1,0.06) -- (1,-0.06);
\node[below,font=\small] at (1,-0.06) {$1$};
\draw (-1,0.06) -- (-1,-0.06);
\node[below,font=\small] at (-1,-0.06) {$-1$};
\draw (0.06,1.5708) -- (-0.06,1.5708);
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.09,1.5708) {$\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\draw (0.06,0.7854) -- (-0.06,0.7854);
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.09,0.7854) {$\frac{\pi}{4}$};
\node[font=\small] at (-0.82,1.35) {$y=\arcsin x$};
\node[font=\small,blue] at (0.78,-0.8) {$y=\arctan x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
